# fixedbugs, defect 014, M-isolated-threads step 5, 2026-09-06 (panel 113 R2).
#
# SYMPTOM: a `[T]` or a `{K: V}` crossed the FFI boundary inside a callback
# signature, in both directions, at **exit 0 with an empty stderr**. The bar was
# one forward declaration and no runtime include:
#
#     struct HeroArrayHeader;
#     void hold(struct HeroArrayHeader *(*mk)(void),
#               void (*run)(struct HeroArrayHeader *));
#
# `heroes build --emit-c` accepted it and wrote `HeroArrayHeader * h_t_make(void);`
# and `void h_t_bump(HeroArrayHeader * h0_xs);`, so C received the header of a
# refcounted Heroes value, could store it, and could hand it to threads of its
# own.
#
# CAUSE: `selfhost/check/ffi.hero`'s `crosses_the_boundary` is the one function
# that decides what a C header may spell. It refuses `.array | .fixed | .map |
# .fallible` and answered `.function_ty => return true` **without recursing into
# that function type's own parameters and result**. So the vocabulary rule was
# applied to the callback and never to what the callback carries.
#
# The specification had already refused it. spec, § FFI: *"A callback is a
# **parameter**, never a result; its parameters follow the same rule"* — and the
# same rule is that function, which refuses `.array` one line below. So this was
# the compiler disagreeing with the spec (CLAUDE.md §12), not a design question,
# and it cost no spec token to settle.
#
# WHY IT MATTERED MORE THAN IT LOOKS. Panel 113 was convened on `cow.c`'s
# `if (refcount == 1)` — a test followed by a mutate — and two seats measured,
# independently, in separate checkouts, with a live positive control, that the
# corruption does NOT arrive through there: with `parts/thread.c`'s guard patched
# down, 8 threads and 240,000 mutations of nested `[[str]]` and `{str: i64}` were
# exit 0 with **zero ThreadSanitizer warnings**, because a callback parameter
# arrives borrowed and the emitted body increfs before it can store. The same
# instrument named a hand-made race at `cow.c:80` in the same session, so its
# silence is admissible. This declaration was the door.
#
# FIX: the `.function_ty` arm recurses through its parameters and its result.
# Eight lines, one file, nothing under `runtime/` or `selfhost/emit/`. It broke
# no program: measured over the whole tree the day it landed, there were **7
# callback declarations inside `extern` groups and 0 of them named a container**.
#
# The header below is `stdlib.h` and the callback is `atexit`'s, deliberately: a
# reader should see that the refusal is about the TYPE and not about the header,
# and this case then needs no C file of its own. The refusal happens in the
# checker, before any probe is compiled.

extern "stdlib.h"
    function atexit(f: (function() -> [i64])) -> i32  #~ ffi_type

function make() -> [i64]
    return [1, 2, 3]

function main()
    _ = atexit(f: make)
